data.address-forms#Address forms:
Autofill returns split fields that map to form inputs.
const a = await (await fetch("https://api.mapx.at/v1/autofill/suggest?q=Herrengasse%2013,%201010%20Wien&limit=3", { headers: { Authorization: "Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" } })).json(); const { address_line1, postcode, place, coordinates } = a.suggestions[0]; Validation checks what the user typed:
curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" "https://api.mapx.at/v1/address/validate?q=Haubtplatz%201,%203390%20Melk" | jq '{status, confidence, address}' status is match, corrected, ambiguous (then candidates[]) or not_found. If the house number does not exist in the street, the result is not_found with the nearest numbers in candidates[]. Abbreviations, umlauts and ß are understood. Use POST with JSON for structured input.
